# bridge-svelte demo — local development configuration
#
# Copy to `.env.local` and adjust. Vite loads `.env.local` automatically and it
# is gitignored, so your app id and local URLs stay on your machine.
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# TBP-121: these used to live in `bridge-plugins/bridge-cli/config/local_overrides.env`,
# a single sourceable file that also carried bridge-cli settings, the
# bridge-nestjs demo's settings, and a long-lived API key in plaintext. Sourcing
# it to run this demo pulled in variables for two unrelated roles and pinned an
# app id documented nowhere. Each consumer now owns its own config, next to the
# thing it configures.

# ── Required ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The Bridge app this demo authenticates against. Find it in the dashboard, or
# create one with `bridge app create`.
#
# Note: the demo prefers `localStorage['bridge:appId']` when present, so the
# in-app app switcher overrides this value. Clear that key to fall back here.
VITE_BRIDGE_APP_ID=

# ── Local stack ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Set both when running against a local bridge-api. Leave unset to use the
# hosted defaults the SDK ships with.
#
# Everything else the SDK needs is derived from these two.
VITE_BRIDGE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3200
VITE_BRIDGE_HOSTED_URL=http://localhost:3091

# ── Optional ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Where the hosted login redirects back to after authentication.
# VITE_BRIDGE_CALLBACK_URL=http://localhost:3001/auth/callback

# Marks the build as production for the SDK's environment checks. Leave unset
# (or `local`) for development.
# VITE_ENVIRONMENT=local
